(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Task-shifting hypertension care to community health workers \(CHWs\) using) Tj
T*
(remote clinical oversight may improve rural access. We explored stakeholder perceptions of) Tj
T*
(CHW-facilitated telehealth versus clinic-based care. Methods: A qualitative substudy) Tj
T*
(nested within the SEARCH Sapphire randomized trial enrolled 40 hypertensive patients and) Tj
T*
(15 healthcare providers in rural Kenya and Uganda. Audio-recorded semi-structured) Tj
T*
(interviews explored experiences with community-based hypertension management, care) Tj
T*
(preferences, and integration of remote consultation into clinical and community workflows.) Tj
T*
(Data were analyzed thematically. Results: Overall, patients in the CHW-remote arm reported) Tj
T*
(satisfaction with community-based care delivery, citing reduced transportation expenses) Tj
T*
(and improved accessibility for those with mobility limitations or distant clinic) Tj
T*
(residence. Patients perceived CHWs as appropriate for routine management and valued) Tj
T*
(clinician involvement in decision-making. Providers noted telehealth consultation quality) Tj
T*
(comparable to in-person care for stable hypertension but acknowledged need for clinic-) Tj
T*
(based evaluation for complex cases. Successful models incorporated clear communication) Tj
T*
(protocols among patients, CHWs, and clinicians. Conclusions: Both patients and providers) Tj
T*
(expressed acceptability of CHW-coordinated remote clinical care as a viable approach to) Tj
T*
(extend hypertension management in resource-limited rural settings, emphasizing the) Tj
T*
(importance of transparent communication and integrated clinical oversight.) Tj
